<title>BELARUS: Belarus seeks $90 mln to convert military airport.</title>
<headline>Belarus seeks $90 mln to convert military airport.</headline>
<dateline>MINSK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belarus is seeking $90 million to convert the Minsk Machulishchi military airport to an international airport and to modernise a local aircraft factory, the planemaker's chief executive said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The airport, which has been serving strategic bombers built in Russia, needs to be converted for civil use but the country does not have the money to do it,&quot; Fyodor Ivanov of the Minsky Aviaremontny Zavod told a news conference.</p>
<p>Ivanon said German airline Lufthansa was investing $500,000 in modernisation of the Minsk-2 international airport in the former Soviet republic.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
